# __SLUG__ scene

The generated geometry is a placeholder, not a recommended story. Before
styling it, write one visible claim and replace the sample state with the real
objects, events, owners, checkpoints, and completion condition.

Register this scene in `src/scenes/index.tsx` by importing the component and
model functions, creating one `SceneDefinition`, and adding it to `scenes`.
The generator prints a ready-to-edit registration block.

Then run:

```bash
./animation svg check
./animation svg capture:checkpoints --scene __SLUG__ --profile fast
./animation svg render:video --scene __SLUG__ --profile fast --output output/__SLUG__-fast.mp4
```

Review [SVG visual direction](../../../references/visual-direction.md) before
polishing the scene.
